<title>UK: Stakis says to sell eight hotels.</title>
<headline>Stakis says to sell eight hotels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scottish-based leisure group Stakis Plc said on Thursday it planned to sell eight hotels which were not compatible with the group's strategy.</p>
<p>The hotels to be sold did not match its planned portfolio of four star full service hotels, the company said.</p>
<p>The company did not say what consideration it was expecting from the sale.</p>
<p>&quot;The proceeds realised will be reinvested in the group's three existing divisions,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
